===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|architecture}} A large [[post]], often used as supporting architecture.
# Something resembling such a structure.
#: {{ux|en|a '''pillar''' of smoke}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An essential part of something that provides support.
#: {{ux|en|He's a '''pillar''' of the community.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1992
|author=w:Richard Nixon
|chapter=The Pacific Triangle
|title=Seize the Moment
|url=https://archive.org/details/seizemomentameri00nixo/
|publisher=w:Simon & Schuster
|ISBN=0-671-74343-0
|LCCN=91-37743
|OCLC=440652941
|page=181
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/seizemomentameri00nixo/page/181/
|text=In the Shanghai Communiqué of 1972, we recognized the fact that both Beijing and Taipei viewed Taiwan as part of China but unequivocally expressed our support for a peaceful settlement of the unification issue. While we should not alter the fundamental '''pillars''' of our policy, we should consider certain steps that will raise Taiwan's international standing.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|actor=Christian Mallen|role=CJ|title=[[w:Manchester by the Sea (film)|Manchester by the Sea]]|writer=w:Kenneth Lonergan|year=2016|text=''Star Trek'' is one of the '''pillars''' of modern entertainment.}}
# {{lb|en|Roman Catholic}} A portable ornamental column, formerly carried before a cardinal, as emblematic of his support to the church.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=a. 1529|author=John Skelton|title=a poem|passage=two laye-men secular<br>eache of theym holdynge a '''pillar''' <br>In their hondes, steade of a mace}}
# The centre of the [[volta]], [[ring]], or [[manege]] ground, around which a [[horse]] turns.
# {{lb|en|bodybuilding}} The [[body]] from the [[hip]]s over the [[core]] to the [[shoulder]]s.
# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[vertical]], often spire-shaped, natural [[rock formation]].

